---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { USCCB_ORDER, USCCB_LEGEND } from '../lib/ratings.js';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Base title="About" description="About the USCCB / Catholic News Service movie reviews archive." active="about">
  <h1>About this archive</h1>
  <p class="lede">A historical archive — coverage runs 1905–2011 and is not updated.</p>

  <p>
    These 13,694 capsule and full-length film reviews were originally published by the
    <strong>USCCB Office for Film &amp; Broadcasting / Catholic News Service</strong>. They were
    parsed from the original archive pages and stored in a single SQLite database, which is
    the source of truth for this site. The collection spans from the early silent era through
    2011, when the archive ends. This site is an independent reference copy and is not
    affiliated with or endorsed by the USCCB; review text remains © its original publishers.
  </p>

  <h2>USCCB rating legend</h2>
  <dl class="dl-list">
    {USCCB_ORDER.map((r) => (
      <>
        <dt><span class="chip usccb">{r}</span></dt>
        <dd>{USCCB_LEGEND[r]}{r === 'A-IV' && ' (older designation, later folded into L)'}</dd>
      </>
    ))}
  </dl>

  <h2>Using the query page</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href={`${base}query`}>Query</a> page lets you run read-only SQL against the database
    entirely in your browser — it fetches only the database pages each query needs via HTTP
    range requests, so there is no server and nothing is uploaded. A few starting points:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Counts by USCCB rating: <code>SELECT cns_rating, COUNT(*) FROM reviews WHERE is_redirect=0 GROUP BY 1;</code></li>
    <li>Full-text search is fastest via <code>reviews_fts MATCH '…'</code> rather than <code>LIKE '%…%'</code>.</li>
    <li>Always add <code>is_redirect=0</code> to exclude the 322 "see other title" pointer stubs.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="note">
    Notes on the data: <code>year</code> is missing for ~3.6% of films and <code>mpaa_rating</code>
    for ~42% (mostly pre-1968 and foreign titles). Full reviews exist for 1,619 films; the rest
    have a short synopsis.
  </p>
</Base>
